{"id":"facsimile","name":"facsimile","aliases":[],"caption":"Document class for preparing faxes","authors":[{"id":"bronger","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Torsten Bronger","year":"2003"}],"license":"lppl1.2","version":{"number":"1.0","date":""},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n        The facsimile class provides a simple interface for creating a\n        document for sending as a fax, with LaTeX. The class covers two\n        areas:\n    <\u002fp>\n  <ul>\n    <li>\n\t  First, a title page is created with a detailed fax\n\t  header;\n\t<\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\t  second, every page gets headers and footers so that\n\t  the recipient can be sure that every page has been received and\n\t  all pages are complete, and in the correct order.\n\t<\u002fli>\n  <\u002ful>\n  <p>\n        The class evolved from the <ref refid=\"fax\">fax<\u002fref> package,\n        and provides much better language support.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/facsimile/facsimile.pdf"},{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/facsimile/README"}],"ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/facsimile","file":true},"miktex":"facsimile","texlive":"facsimile","topics":["letter","class"]}